{"topic": "Gradient Descent and Learning Rate", "audience": "", "referenceMaterial": "[none provided]", "allowedTypes": {"chart": "Author a chart block for a LectureDoc lecture — a data chart (bar/line/area/scatter) rendered via Observable Plot, theme-aware. Reach for it whenever a page shows numeric comparison, trend over time, share/composition, or correlation — anything where seeing the shape of the numbers beats reading them. Prefer a chart over a table when magnitude/trend/relationship is the point; use a table only for exact nominal lookup where values are not being compared. Produces schema-valid chart block JSON.", "runnable": "Author a runnable (edit → Run) code cell block for a LectureDoc lecture — an in-browser Python (Pyodide) + JavaScript editor with a console and a result chart. Reach for it whenever the student should learn by writing/modifying and actually executing code themselves: implementing an algorithm by hand, tuning parameters and seeing the effect, exploratory what-if coding. Use a plain `code` block instead for read-only display the student will not run. Produces schema-valid runnable block JSON.", "hero": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "statement": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "pullquote": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "list": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "agenda": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "callout": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "formula": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "flow": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "table": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "code": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "compare": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "grid": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "timeline": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "freeform": "Author a freeform block for a LectureDoc lecture — the long-tail fallback for a visual relationship that none of the formal block types can express, drawn as inline SVG/HTML restricted to theme colour tokens. Reach for it only after checking the structured types: graph covers trees, DAGs and branching flowcharts; chart covers data; diagram covers fixed shapes; grid and sim.widget cover custom layouts and interactive pieces. When it genuinely is the right tool it now renders as normal page content, so use it without hedging. Produces schema-valid freeform block JSON.", "stats": "Author stats (KPI number cards), diagram (fixed structural shapes — cycle/pyramid/staircase/snake/arrow-seq/circular-grid/connected-circles) and graph (true node-edge trees, DAGs and branching flowcharts, rendered as real layered SVG) blocks for a LectureDoc lecture. Reach for stats to spotlight a handful of standalone key numbers; reach for graph whenever nodes have *named relationships* — parent/child, dependency, branch, merge — since it is the only block type with an edges field; reach for diagram only for a fixed decorative shape with no explicit edges. Use flow for a simple linear 2-3 step sequence. Produces schema-valid stats/diagram/graph block JSON.", "diagram": "Author stats (KPI number cards), diagram (fixed structural shapes — cycle/pyramid/staircase/snake/arrow-seq/circular-grid/connected-circles) and graph (true node-edge trees, DAGs and branching flowcharts, rendered as real layered SVG) blocks for a LectureDoc lecture. Reach for stats to spotlight a handful of standalone key numbers; reach for graph whenever nodes have *named relationships* — parent/child, dependency, branch, merge — since it is the only block type with an edges field; reach for diagram only for a fixed decorative shape with no explicit edges. Use flow for a simple linear 2-3 step sequence. Produces schema-valid stats/diagram/graph block JSON.", "graph": "Author stats (KPI number cards), diagram (fixed structural shapes — cycle/pyramid/staircase/snake/arrow-seq/circular-grid/connected-circles) and graph (true node-edge trees, DAGs and branching flowcharts, rendered as real layered SVG) blocks for a LectureDoc lecture. Reach for stats to spotlight a handful of standalone key numbers; reach for graph whenever nodes have *named relationships* — parent/child, dependency, branch, merge — since it is the only block type with an edges field; reach for diagram only for a fixed decorative shape with no explicit edges. Use flow for a simple linear 2-3 step sequence. Produces schema-valid stats/diagram/graph block JSON.", "quiz": "Author a quiz block for a LectureDoc lecture — objective (multiple-choice, auto-graded) or subjective (open discussion prompt). Reach for it whenever a page should check understanding or provoke reflection rather than only present — at least one per lecture is encouraged. Objective for a checkable fact/skill, subjective for open-ended thinking. Produces schema-valid quiz block JSON.", "sim": "Author a sim (simulation) block for a LectureDoc lecture — a parameter-driven interactive that recomputes and redraws in-browser as the student changes inputs. Reach for it whenever a quantitative or mechanistic process becomes clearer by letting the student turn a knob and watch the outcome change (physics/chem dynamics, algorithm behaviour, parameter sensitivity); pick a sim over a static chart when the interaction itself is the teaching point. Engines are chosen at build time: dynamics1d/searchCompare (declarative restricted-expression math → line charts), custom (sandboxed compute), widget (live canvas/SVG animation, geometric construction, or arbitrary mouse interaction). Skip it when the topic has no quantifiable/mechanistic process to manipulate — a sim with no real parameter to turn is decoration, not interaction. Produces schema-valid sim block JSON."}, "currentBrief": {"objective": "学生能比较不同学习率下梯度下降的收敛行为，并解释过大/过小学习率的影响", "keyClaim": "学习率过大导致震荡/发散，过小导致收敛极慢，需要折中选择", "misconception": "", "visualTask": "视觉直接编码本页核心关系", "evidencePolicy": "none"}, "currentScene": {"id": "learning-rate-tradeoff", "kind": "content", "headline": "学习率 η：太大跳过谷底，太小停滞不前", "lead": "学习率 η 控制梯度下降每一步的步长，是影响收敛行为的关键超参数。", "notes": "图表中 η=0.001 收敛极慢，η=0.1 快速收敛，η=1.0 震荡发散；经验法则范围 0.001~0.1 需结合具体问题调整。", "blocks": [{"type": "sim", "engine": "widget", "html": "<style>
  .lr-widget { background: var(--bg2); border-radius: var(--radius, 12px); padding: 16px; color: var(--ink); height: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .lr-widget canvas { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 680px; height: auto; margin: 0 auto; background: var(--card); border-radius: var(--radius, 8px); flex: 1; min-height: 0; }
  .controls { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 8px 16px; margin-top: 12px; }
  .ctrl-group { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
  .ctrl-group label { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text2); white-space: nowrap; }
  .ctrl-group input[type=range] { width: 80px; accent-color: var(--accent); cursor: pointer; }
  .ctrl-group .val { font-family: var(--mono); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; font-size: 12px; color: var(--accent); min-width: 36px; text-align: right; }
  .ctrl-group .dot { display: inline-block; width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; margin-right: 2px; }
  .btn-row { display: flex; gap: 8px; margin-left: auto; }
  .btn-row button { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--ink); font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 12px; padding: 4px 12px; border-radius: var(--radius, 6px); cursor: pointer; transition: background 150ms, border-color 150ms; }
  .btn-row button:hover { background: var(--bg2); border-color: var(--accent); }
  .btn-row button:active { background: var(--accent); color: var(--bg); }
  .readout { display: flex; gap: 16px; margin-top: 8px; font-size: 11px; color: var(--text2); flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .readout .item { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; }
  .readout .item .mono { font-family: var(--mono); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; color: var(--ink); }
</style>
<div class="lr-widget">
  <canvas id="stage" width="680" height="360"></canvas>
  <div class="controls">
    <div class="ctrl-group">
      <span class="dot" style="background:var(--accent); opacity:0.8"></span>
      <label for="lr1">η₁</label>
      <input type="range" id="lr1" min="0.01" max="0.5" step="0.01" value="0.1">
      <span class="val mono" id="lr1Val">0.10</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl-group">
      <span class="dot" style="background:var(--accent); opacity:0.5"></span>
      <label for="lr2">η₂</label>
      <input type="range" id="lr2" min="0.01" max="0.5" step="0.01" value="0.8">
      <span class="val mono" id="lr2Val">0.80</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl-group">
      <span class="dot" style="background:var(--accent); opacity:0.3"></span>
      <label for="lr3">η₃</label>
      <input type="range" id="lr3" min="0.01" max="0.5" step="0.01" value="0.01">
      <span class="val mono" id="lr3Val">0.01</span>
    </div>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <button id="play-pause">⏸</button>
      <button id="reset">↺</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="readout">
    <div class="item"><span class="dot" style="background:var(--accent); opacity:0.8"></span>η=0.10 步数 <span class="mono" id="step1Display">1</span> x=<span class="mono" id="x1Display">1.44</span></div>
    <div class="item"><span class="dot" style="background:var(--accent); opacity:0.5"></span>η=0.80 步数 <span class="mono" id="step2Display">1</span> x=<span class="mono" id="x2Display">-1.08</span></div>
    <div class="item"><span class="dot" style="background:var(--accent); opacity:0.3"></span>η=0.01 步数 <span class="mono" id="step3Display">1</span> x=<span class="mono" id="x3Display">1.76</span></div>
  </div>
</div>
<script>
  (function() {
    const root = document.documentElement;
    const tok = n => getComputedStyle(root).getPropertyValue(n).trim();
    const canvas = document.getElementById('stage');
    const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
    const W = 680, H = 360;
    const margin = { top: 20, bottom: 30, left: 40, right: 20 };
    const plotW = W - margin.left - margin.right;
    const plotH = H - margin.top - margin.bottom;
    const xMin = -2.2, xMax = 2.2;
    const yMin = -0.5, yMax = 4.5;
    function toScreen(x, y) {
      const sx = margin.left + (x - xMin) / (xMax - xMin) * plotW;
      const sy = margin.top + (yMax - y) / (yMax - yMin) * plotH;
      return [sx, sy];
    }

    let lr1 = 0.1, lr2 = 0.8, lr3 = 0.01;
    let step1 = 1, step2 = 1, step3 = 1;
    let x1 = 1.44, x2 = -1.08, x3 = 1.764;
    let running = true;
    const maxSteps = 30;
    const startX = 1.8;

    let hist1 = [startX], hist2 = [startX], hist3 = [startX];
    hist1.push(x1); hist2.push(x2); hist3.push(x3);

    const lr1Input = document.getElementById('lr1');
    const lr2Input = document.getElementById('lr2');
    const lr3Input = document.getElementById('lr3');
    const lr1Val = document.getElementById('lr1Val');
    const lr2Val = document.getElementById('lr2Val');
    const lr3Val = document.getElementById('lr3Val');
    const step1D = document.getElementById('step1Display');
    const step2D = document.getElementById('step2Display');
    const step3D = document.getElementById('step3Display');
    const x1D = document.getElementById('x1Display');
    const x2D = document.getElementById('x2Display');
    const x3D = document.getElementById('x3Display');
    const playBtn = document.getElementById('play-pause');
    const resetBtn = document.getElementById('reset');

    function updateReadouts() {
      lr1Val.textContent = lr1.toFixed(2);
      lr2Val.textContent = lr2.toFixed(2);
      lr3Val.textContent = lr3.toFixed(2);
      step1D.textContent = step1;
      step2D.textContent = step2;
      step3D.textContent = step3;
      x1D.textContent = x1.toFixed(2);
      x2D.textContent = x2.toFixed(2);
      x3D.textContent = x3.toFixed(2);
    }

    function draw() {
      const ink = tok('--ink');
      const accent = tok('--accent');
      const line = tok('--line');
      const muted = tok('--text2');
      const bg = tok('--card');

      ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
      ctx.fillStyle = bg;
      ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);

      ctx.strokeStyle = line;
      ctx.lineWidth = 0.5;
      ctx.setLineDash([3, 4]);
      for (let x = -2; x <= 2; x += 0.5) {
        const [sx] = toScreen(x, 0);
        ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(sx, margin.top); ctx.lineTo(sx, margin.top + plotH); ctx.stroke();
      }
      for (let y = 0; y <= 4; y += 0.5) {
        const [, sy] = toScreen(0, y);
        ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(margin.left, sy); ctx.lineTo(margin.left + plotW, sy); ctx.stroke();
      }
      ctx.setLineDash([]);

      ctx.strokeStyle = muted;
      ctx.lineWidth = 1;
      const [ax0, ay0] = toScreen(0, 0);
      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(margin.left, ay0); ctx.lineTo(margin.left + plotW, ay0); ctx.stroke();
      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(ax0, margin.top); ctx.lineTo(ax0, margin.top + plotH); ctx.stroke();

      ctx.fillStyle = muted;
      ctx.font = '10px ' + tok('--mono');
      ctx.textAlign = 'center';
      for (let x = -2; x <= 2; x += 0.5) {
        if (x === 0) continue;
        const [sx] = toScreen(x, 0);
        ctx.fillText(x.toFixed(1), sx, margin.top + plotH + 14);
      }
      ctx.textAlign = 'right';
      for (let y = 0; y <= 4; y += 0.5) {
        if (y === 0) continue;
        const [, sy] = toScreen(0, y);
        ctx.fillText(y.toFixed(1), margin.left - 6, sy + 3);
      }

      ctx.strokeStyle = ink;
      ctx.lineWidth = 1.5;
      ctx.beginPath();
      for (let px = 0; px <= plotW; px += 1) {
        const x = xMin + px / plotW * (xMax - xMin);
        const y = x * x;
        const [sx, sy] = toScreen(x, y);
        if (px === 0) ctx.moveTo(sx, sy); else ctx.lineTo(sx, sy);
      }
      ctx.stroke();

      function drawTrajectory(hist, alpha, currentX, currentY) {
        if (hist.length < 2) return;
        ctx.strokeStyle = accent;
        ctx.lineWidth = 1.2;
        ctx.globalAlpha = alpha * 0.5;
        ctx.beginPath();
        for (let i = 0; i < hist.length; i++) {
          const y = hist[i] * hist[i];
          const [sx, sy] = toScreen(hist[i], y);
          if (i === 0) ctx.moveTo(sx, sy); else ctx.lineTo(sx, sy);
        }
        ctx.stroke();
        ctx.globalAlpha = 1;

        for (let i = 0; i < hist.length; i++) {
          const y = hist[i] * hist[i];
          const [sx, sy] = toScreen(hist[i], y);
          ctx.fillStyle = accent;
          ctx.globalAlpha = i === hist.length - 1 ? alpha : alpha * 0.3;
          ctx.beginPath();
          ctx.arc(sx, sy, i === hist.length - 1 ? 5 : 3, 0, Math.PI * 2);
          ctx.fill();
        }
        ctx.globalAlpha = 1;

        ctx.fillStyle = accent;
        ctx.globalAlpha = alpha;
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(currentX, currentY, 7, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.fill();
        ctx.strokeStyle = bg;
        ctx.lineWidth = 2;
        ctx.stroke();
        ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
      }

      const [cx1, cy1] = toScreen(x1, x1 * x1);
      const [cx2, cy2] = toScreen(x2, x2 * x2);
      const [cx3, cy3] = toScreen(x3, x3 * x3);

      drawTrajectory(hist1, 0.8, cx1, cy1);
      drawTrajectory(hist2, 0.5, cx2, cy2);
      drawTrajectory(hist3, 0.3, cx3, cy3);

      ctx.font = '11px ' + tok('--mono');
      ctx.textAlign = 'left';
      ctx.fillStyle = accent;
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.8;
      ctx.fillText('η=0.10', margin.left + 8, margin.top + 16);
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.5;
      ctx.fillText('η=0.80', margin.left + 8, margin.top + 32);
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.3;
      ctx.fillText('η=0.01', margin.left + 8, margin.top + 48);
      ctx.globalAlpha = 1;

      ctx.fillStyle = muted;
      ctx.textAlign = 'right';
      ctx.fillText('步数 ' + step1, margin.left + plotW - 8, margin.top + 16);
      ctx.fillText('步数 ' + step2, margin.left + plotW - 8, margin.top + 32);
      ctx.fillText('步数 ' + step3, margin.left + plotW - 8, margin.top + 48);
    }

    function update() {
      if (running) {
        if (step1 < maxSteps) {
          const grad1 = 2 * x1;
          x1 = x1 - lr1 * grad1;
          step1++;
          hist1.push(x1);
        }
        if (step2 < maxSteps) {
          const grad2 = 2 * x2;
          x2 = x2 - lr2 * grad2;
          step2++;
          hist2.push(x2);
        }
        if (step3 < maxSteps) {
          const grad3 = 2 * x3;
          x3 = x3 - lr3 * grad3;
          step3++;
          hist3.push(x3);
        }
        if (step1 >= maxSteps && step2 >= maxSteps && step3 >= maxSteps) {
          running = false;
          playBtn.textContent = '▶';
        }
      }
      updateReadouts();
      draw();
    }

    lr1Input.addEventListener('input', function() {
      lr1 = parseFloat(this.value);
      step1 = 0; x1 = startX; hist1 = [startX];
      if (!running) { running = true; playBtn.textContent = '⏸'; }
      update();
    });
    lr2Input.addEventListener('input', function() {
      lr2 = parseFloat(this.value);
      step2 = 0; x2 = startX; hist2 = [startX];
      if (!running) { running = true; playBtn.textContent = '⏸'; }
      update();
    });
    lr3Input.addEventListener('input', function() {
      lr3 = parseFloat(this.value);
      step3 = 0; x3 = startX; hist3 = [startX];
      if (!running) { running = true; playBtn.textContent = '⏸'; }
      update();
    });

    playBtn.addEventListener('click', function() {
      running = !running;
      this.textContent = running ? '⏸' : '▶';
      if (running) update();
    });

    resetBtn.addEventListener('click', function() {
      step1 = 0; step2 = 0; step3 = 0;
      x1 = startX; x2 = startX; x3 = startX;
      hist1 = [startX]; hist2 = [startX]; hist3 = [startX];
      running = true;
      playBtn.textContent = '⏸';
      update();
    });

    update();

    let lastTime = performance.now();
    function loop(time) {
      const dt = time - lastTime;
      lastTime = time;
      if (running && dt > 16) {
        update();
      }
      requestAnimationFrame(loop);
    }
    requestAnimationFrame(loop);
